  "details": "There have been users who display obscene images using custom emojis for some time now. I can hide them by setting a custom shield level, but there should be a function to hide custom emojis and emojis in bulk in the first place.\n\nA function to hide all stickers is also necessary. There is a function to hide all stickers, but I have to hide them every time I enter an instance. An option to hide them permanently is necessary.\n\nI had been putting up with these issues, but the newly added ‘Items’ feature get me mad. To hide the items, I have to hide each one individually. What's more, the items can be rearranged, so I have to hide them each time I do so. There is no option to hide them all at once, and I can't even hide them with a custom shield level.\n\nThe reason I hate these emojis, stickers, and items is that they get in the way in the game world. I can't see what's behind the items, and the items someone holds in them hands hide the real weapons they have. And above all, it's really distracting to have things that are unrelated to the game in my field of vision.\n\nThink about it. What would happen if vrc added these features to an FPS game played in e-sports? They’d be a huge distraction. Of course, the vrc features themselves aren’t bad. The problem is that there’s no option to hide them all at once.\n\nWhen adding new features, don’t forget to include an option to hide them as well.",
